  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 200C. Cut the cauliflower into small florets. Drain and rinse half the chickpeas. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/149190/photos/large/prep_ingredients-9e64c2e6c992d5bdd14abf0dad93b3f6.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast cauliflower: Put the cauliflower and chickpeas in a medium roasting pan. Combine the garlic, 2 tsp ras el hanout and 1 tbs olive oil in a bowl. Drizzle over the cauliflower and chickpeas, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat. Roast, turning halfway, for 30 mins or until tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/149191/photos/large/roast_cauliflower-f825f49c1bb8154808064bf47eb54ca7.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast almonds: Meanwhile, put the almonds in a cold small frypan over medium heat. Toast, tossing, for 3-4 mins until evenly golden. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/149192/photos/large/toast_almonds-71a733d69bf28de47c450f979d68b0d0.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make dressing: Put the yoghurt, 2 tsp red wine vinegar and 2 tsp honey in a bowl. Season with salt and pepper and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/149193/photos/large/make_dressing-44098e00d425aec95ee67761edb09c84.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the spinach, currants, almonds and yoghurt dressing to the roasted cauliflower and chickpeas and toss to combine. Divide among bowls and enjoy.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/149194/photos/large/toss_salad_and_serve_up-eae72cbdbc04b149cd38949722ab44ca.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know?: Ras el hanout is a North African blend of aromatic spices, often including ground coriander seeds, cumin, cardamom and ginger. Its Arabic name translates as 'head of the shop', meaning the mix contains all the best spices in the shop – with some blends made up with over twenty different spices.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/149195/photos/large/did_you_know-386330b870761754840a47a82f2ad8cb.jpeg"
    }
  ]
